# - Serato, The Drop, Studio 2.0 Artist Profile: Boston Chery (opened 2026-10-20, published 2023-04-04): Boston-born, Brooklyn-based DJ and producer; founded The 8th Path, a label highlighting BIPOC producers and DJs around the world; Afro-Caribbean club music; grew up in New York City, beatboxing to passing cars and trains; Haitian background, Kompa and the tanbou; producing in high school on Soundtrack Pro by manipulating its loops; self described sample producer; influences Darkchild, Timbaland, Missy Elliott, Kaytranada, High Klassified, TRAKGIRL, Nova Wave, Melo-X, Haitian Kompa music; music style listed as percussive, colorful, Caribbean; setup Serato Studio with AKAI MPK.
# - Rooftop Films, Citizen Ashe event page (opened 2026-10-20, event June 28, 2022): Boston Chery, pronounced Cherie, Boston-bred, Haitian-American, Brooklyn-based DJ and producer; love of 90s reggae, dancehall, Afrobeat, world music, R&B and hip hop; performed on Boiler Room and Sway In The Morning on XM radio; member of Splice inaugural Creator Class; appeared at AFROPUNK, the Brooklyn Museum and Boston Museum of Fine Arts; shared stages with Jill Scott, Kaytranada, GoldLink and MeLo-X; residencies at Dumbo House in Brooklyn and Peachy bar in Chinatown.
# - Earth in Color, Radicle Sounds interview (opened 2026-10-20, published 2023-09-08): in her own words, DJ, producer and event curator; born in Massachusetts, from New York, grew up in Crown Heights, Brooklyn; writing music and beatboxing learned from her mother at seven; the DJ idea from a friend mother in elementary school; producing in high school on Soundtrack Pro; DJing officially in college on Virtual DJ, first gigs at birthday and house parties, DJing off the stove; 2012 Soho period, internship at Global Grind, DJing for Mass Appeal, mentor Natasha Diggs gave a residency at the DL Rooftop and Lounge; flown to Art Basel, first flight, crowd of over 1,000; DJing for the queer community, queer Haitians thanking her, representation; cooking playlist arc from Afrobeats to amapiano, R&B and NOLA bounce; dish of home: diri kole.
# - Serato, The Drop, Serato Paradise 2026 (opened 2026-10-20): Brooklyn-based DJ, label founder, child of the Haitian diaspora; The Eighth Path, label and platform dedicated to platforming BIPOC DJs and producers globally, name from born on the 8th, life path number eight and the Buddhist Eightfold Path; the label has booked DJs from Australia to Japan, Guadeloupe to Austria; sets move between Haitian Kompa, Caribbean rhythms, Raboday and new electronic R&B; Apple Music mix opening in Kompa and Caribbean sounds; mentor Natasha Diggs story retold; invited with Mike Taylor and YO! MAFIA to create Apple Music mixes on Serato curator page.
# - Splice, Meet the Creator Class of 2019 (search result, 2026-10-20): Boston Chery, DJ and producer, 10 years of DJ experience and 4 years of production experience at that date, afrobeat, dancehall and hip hop influences. Used only to corroborate the inaugural Creator Class point already stated by Rooftop Films.
# Note: Boston Chery is not a bouyon artist by catalogue. She is on this site for one explicit, self labelled bouyon fact: her Bandcamp head release, Spend It, is titled a Boston Chery Bouyon Remix of Summer Walker. The rest of her catalogue is Afro-Caribbean club music, edits and R&B and hip hop remixes, and this profile keeps that boundary exact.

